    "heading": "finStatus values",
    "anchor": "finstatus-values",
    "level": 2,
    "content": "Never retry before confirming the outcome Retrying a sale before confirming the previous transaction was not charged risks double-charging the cardholder. Always obtain a final non- status from the recovery flow before initiating a new sale. PAX Android — duplicate check screen: If the same physical card is tapped again during a potential retry, the Handpoint Payments App shows a \"Duplicate transaction — Cancel or Accept\" prompt to the cardholder. This is a last-resort safeguard, not a replacement for status recovery. Passing skips this prompt entirely and is not recommended."
