    "level": 3,
    "content": "Generate the UUID before initiating the transaction and write it to durable storage. If your app crashes immediately after calling but before fires, you can still recover because the reference was persisted first. Use a UUID v4. Generate a new UUID for every transaction — including retries. Reusing a UUID from a previous attempt can cause the gateway to treat the retry as the same operation."
