    "heading": "deviceready — recover after WebView reload",
    "anchor": "deviceready-recover-after-webview-reload",
    "level": 3,
    "content": "If the WebView is restarted by the OS or by a plugin, all in-memory state is lost. Check persistent storage as soon as Cordova is ready: Clear the stored reference once recovery resolves: localStorage reliability survives WebView reloads on most platforms but may be cleared under OS storage pressure or in private browsing mode. Always mirror the reference to your backend in — the REST recovery path () works without any SDK or device connection. Partial approvals (US only) If is , the device may be showing an accept/decline prompt to the cardholder with approximately a 30-second timeout. The 60-second wait built into the background recovery above covers this window. Do not act on a partial approval result immediately — always allow the full wait period to elapse."
