    "level": 2,
    "content": "A sealed factory class that creates and returns the single instance. Call once during app startup and store the result. Static method Returns the instance. If called again in the same process lifetime, the existing instance is returned unchanged. Example is a singleton internally — only one is created per process. If you call a second time, the original instance is returned. To switch credentials you must restart the process."
